  abstract = {Clinical details of 74 consecutive patients for whom plasma PTH radioimmunoassay was requested were reviewed. Plasma PTH was elevated in 39 patients, including 19 patients with primary hyperparathyroidism (25\%), 15 patients with secondary hyperparathyroidism (11 patients with renal failure = 15\% and 4 patients with osteomalacia = 5\%), and 6 'normocalcaemic' renal stone formers (9\%). The PTH radioimmunoassay is a valuable test in the diagnosis of hyperparathyroidism and in helping to distinguish between nonparathyroid hypercalcaemia and primary hyperparathyroidism, between hyperparathyroid and 'idiopathic' renal stone formers, and between osteomalacia and osteoporosis},
