models, a history of proteinuria remained an independent marker of increased infection risk for LRTI, pneumonia, and sepsis (IRRs of 1.07 [95\% CI, 1.05-1.09], 1.26 [95\% CI, 1.19-1.33], and 1.33 [95\% CI, 1.20-1.47]). LIMITATIONS: Patients without creatinine results were excluded. CONCLUSIONS: Strategies to prevent infection among people with CKD are needed.},
