  abstract = {Resume Vingt infections urinaires {\`a} Staphylococcus aureus r{\'e}sistant {\`a} la m{\'e}ticilline dont treize sur sonde v{\'e}sicale ont {\'e}t{\'e} trait{\'e}es par 2 grammes d'Augmentin{\textregistered} per os et par jour. Les examens cyto-bact{\'e}riologiques des urines de contr{\^o}le faits {\`a} J3 ont {\'e}t{\'e} n{\'e}gatifs pour les vingt malades trait{\'e}s. Le succ{\`e}s th{\'e}rapeutique a pu {\^e}tre confirm{\'e} au long cours pour quatorze des dix-sept malades qui ont {\'e}t{\'e} suivis au moins un mois. Une seule souche est apparue r{\'e}sistante h{\'e}t{\'e}rog{\`e}ne {\`a} la m{\'e}ticilline et quatre {\'e}taient non productrices de {$\beta$}-lactamase. Les CMI 90 de l'amoxicilline et de l'ampicilline {\'e}taient {\'e}gales {\`a} 32 mg/l et l'adjonction in vitro de 400 mg/l d'acide clavulanique et de 100 mg/l de sulbactam ont permis d'obtenir des CMI de ces deux p{\'e}nicillines A inf{\'e}rieures ou {\'e}gales {\`a} 4 mg/l pour respectivement quinze et dix-huit souches. Le dosage urinaire de l'amoxicilline et de l'acide clavulanique fait chez six malades deux heures apr{\`e}s la prise d'un gramme d'Augmentin{\textregistered} varie d'un malade {\`a} l'autre et peut {\^e}tre extr{\^e}mement faible {\`a} la 12{\`e}me heure. Au sein d'un m{\^e}me ph{\'e}notype de r{\'e}sistance aux anti-staphylococciques, le comportement des souches vis-{\`a}-vis des {$\beta$}-lactamines et de leur association aux inhibiteurs de {$\beta$}-lactamases peut {\^e}tre diff{\'e}rent. Ce sont les souches les plus r{\'e}sistantes aux p{\'e}nicillines A qui sont impliqu{\'e}es dans les trois {\'e}checs. Summary Twenty patients with urinary tract infections (13 catheter-related) were treated orally with 2 g of Augmentin{\textregistered} per day. Cytobacteriological analysis of urine samples at day 3 of treatment were negative in every case. Therapeutic success was confirmed in 14 of the 17 patients who were followed for at least one month. Only one strain was heterogeneously resistant to methicillin, and four did not produce betalactamase. The MIC 90 values for amoxycillin and ampicillin were 32 mg/l and the addition in vitro of 400 mg/l of clavulanic acid and 100 mg/l of sulbactam reduced the MICs to {$\leq$} 4 mg/l in respectively 15 and 18 strains. Urinary concentrations of amoxycillin and clavulanic acid in six patients two hours after ingestion of 1 g of Augmentin{\textregistered} varied from one patient to another and were very low at 12 h in some cases. The behavior of strains belonging to a given antistaphylococcal drug resistance phenotype towards betalactams alone and in combination with betalactamase inhibitors was variable. The isolates involved in the three treatment failures belonged to the group of strains with the highest level of resistance to penicillin A.},
